A||N||5||V8Dreamer||Isuzu 5spd fluid???||||1||
Z||000000||V8Dreamer||07-16-2001||03:23 PM||||I was just wondering what most people filled their trannys with....I know GM sells a product called synchro-mesh, and was thinking about spending the $$ to get it, that is unless someone tells me it's just motor oil in a fancy container.  So, what do YOU use?<P>Thanks,<BR>Ryan||||reg||1
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||07-16-2001||04:27 PM||||I've always used the motor oil in the past with no problems however there was some discussion on this topic a week or two ago some people claim that the fancy oil you are talking about helps things slide together smoother so when I find some time to change the oil in my tranny I will be switching over to the syncro oil ||||reg||1
Z||000002||StuGood||07-16-2001||06:08 PM||||The GM Synchromesh Fluid is recommended (by GM) for the 5-speed Getrag transaxle.  I don't remember it being recommended for the 5-speed Isuzu.  It's possible someone on the Forum has used Synchromesh Fluid in an Isuzu, but I don't recall.<P>I am least familiar with the Isuzu transaxles (vs. the Muncies, Getrags, and automatics).  In other words, I have very little experience with the Isuzus myself (own one, drive it the least), so others may have better advice to offer.  However, my thinking is, if you're happy with the way your Isuzu behaves using motor oil (or whatever the recommended lube is), I would probably stay with it.<P>Caveat:  I really don't know how the different lubes might affect durability.||||reg||4
Z||000003||V8Dreamer||07-17-2001||10:21 AM||||Anybody else out there with an isuzu..... I know we're not the only ones, your opinions please guys.<P>Thanks,<BR>Ryan||||reg||1
Z||000004||ChadMan||07-17-2001||10:31 AM||||Plain ol' Valvoline 5w30 motor oil.  Slick shifts and no Cap'n Crunch sounds, even at 125K miles.<P>When I bought my 88 Coupe, I was afraid the Isuzu would be the weak link in the drivetrain.  After all this troublefree service and hearing everybody's 2.8/3.1/3.4/SBC testimonials, I'm a believer in the Isuzu transaxle.<p>[This message has been edited by ChadMan (edited 07-17-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000005||artherd||07-18-2001||09:35 PM||||I was pretty happy with "plain oil" in the transaxles, I switched to RedLine MTL, and now I am REALLY REALLY HAPPY :P)<P>best, <BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
